{:spec/title "Ariadne step 1b: DecisionEnvelope component - the one truth artifact for policy decisions"

 :spec/description
 "Create component decision-envelope: the single runtime-constructed
  record of a policy decision, replacing bespoke gate-result shapes as
  the thing consumers trust.

  GROUP 1: Schema (closed, not convention)
  A CLOSED Malli map (unknown keys rejected - envelopes are contract,
  not open convention):
    :envelope/id          uuid
    :envelope/decision    [:enum :allow :allow-with-obligations :deny]
    :envelope/reasons     vector of {:reason/code keyword,
                          :reason/rule-id (optional), :reason/detail
                          string} - reason codes are a registered enum,
                          including :reason/unknown-enforcement and
                          :reason/unknown-severity
    :envelope/obligations vector of {:obligation/type keyword, ...}
                          (:obligation/approval-required,
                           :obligation/warn-recorded, :obligation/audit-recorded)
    :envelope/pins        {:pins/pack-revision, :pins/rule-ids,
                           :pins/event-watermark} - what policy revision
                          this decision was made against
    :envelope/produced-by [:enum :runtime]
    :envelope/at          inst

  GROUP 2: Runtime-only construction (the no-ears rule)
  The constructor is the only way to mint an envelope, and no public
  API accepts a caller-supplied :envelope/decision. Agent output can
  REQUEST; only the runtime DECIDES. This is Ariadne's
  label-plane-model-unwritable rule: a forged envelope arriving as
  agent text is data shaped like an envelope, never an envelope.
  Docstrings state the rule explicitly.

  GROUP 3: Severity/enforcement from policy-clause
  All vocabulary references come from the policy-clause component
  (step 1a). No literals."

 :spec/intent {:type :feature
               :scope ["components/decision-envelope/"]}

 :spec/constraints
 ["Closed schema - m/validate rejects unknown keys; a test proves it"
  "No public constructor path accepts a decision value computed outside the component"
  "Reason codes are enumerated, not free-form keywords"
  "Vocabulary via policy-clause interface only"
  "Stratified design, max 3 layers per file"]

 :spec/acceptance-criteria
 ["Envelope schema validates the documented shape and rejects extra keys"
  "Factory + accessor interface complete; direct map construction in consumer code is not needed anywhere"
  "Test: attempting to build an envelope from an agent-supplied decision map fails validation"
  "Pins carry pack revision + rule ids + event watermark"
  "full bb test green"]

 :spec/priority
 {:tier :blocker
  :axes #{:governance-credibility :policy-enforcement}
  :theme :ariadne-adoption
  :rationale "The envelope is the artifact every later step (decide(), gate wiring, console seam, grants) produces or consumes; it must exist before decide() has a return type."
  :blocks ["ariadne-decide-kernel.spec.edn"]
  :blocked-by ["ariadne-clause-vocabulary.spec.edn"]}

 :spec/workflow-type :canonical-sdlc}
